2. Python Basics
Python is the most widely used language in data science because of its readable syntax and its ecosystem of libraries (NumPy, pandas, SciPy, scikit-learn, Matplotlib).
2.1 Variables and Built-in Types
Python is dynamically typed: a variable takes the type of the value assigned to it. The four most common scalar types are int, float, str and bool.
