2.3 Control Flow, Functions and Comprehensions
def grade(score):
    if score >= 90:
        return "A"
    elif score >= 75:
        return "B"
    return "C"
 
def mean(values):
    return sum(values) / len(values)
 
grades = [grade(s) for s in scores]   # list comprehension
print(grades)
print(mean(scores))
['C', 'B', 'A', 'C', 'B']
79.6

Functions keep code reusable and testable, and list comprehensions express a transformation in a single readable line. Loops (for, while) and conditionals (if / elif / else) complete the basic control-flow toolkit.
