3.3 Structured vs. Unstructured Data
Structured: rows and columns with a fixed schema (SQL tables, CSV files).
Semi-structured: flexible but tagged (JSON, XML).
Unstructured: no predefined schema (text, images, audio, video).

Setting correct dtypes in pandas saves memory, prevents wrong calculations (for example averaging a numeric code that is really a category) and makes ordering explicit:
